    51	`rx_queue_count()` (`helpers.rs:834`) / `userspaceRXQueueCount()`
    52	(`interfaces.go:481`) still count `/sys/class/net/<if>/queues/rx-*`
    53	verbatim. On virtio_net there is **no** structural reservation that makes
    54	the bindable set smaller than the sysfs `rx-*` count (the issue body's
    55	"virtio reserves queue pairs for XDP_TX" hypothesis was retracted in the
    56	issue's own deep-research comment: virtio supports per-queue binding
    57	`0..N-1`). After the `016bc7634` dedup removed the duplicate-netdev
    58	over-count, sysfs count == bindable count on virtio, and all queues bind
    59	(proven by the #1929 5000pps flood across all bindings). So the raw-sysfs
    60	enumeration is **benign** here. Defect A as a forwarding cause is dead.
