docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2020:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:2568:No dataplane-side liveness deadline/watchdog enforces fail-closed when control plane stops making progress.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2021:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:2573:- systemd watchdog/fencing integration that deterministically disables local forwarding state
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2025:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6641:## #349 — HA watchdog sync is throttled past the helper stale-after threshold [CLOSED] (closed 2026-04-02)
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2026:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6643:The current userspace HA watchdog cadence is internally inconsistent.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2027:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6646:- `pkg/dataplane/userspace/manager.go:4792-4798` throttles watchdog-only HA sync to the helper to once every `5*time.Second`
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2028:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6648:- helper forwarding logic treats any RG with an older watchdog timestamp as `HAInactive` in:
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2029:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6653:- The manager can intentionally wait 5 seconds before pushing a fresh watchdog timestamp.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2030:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6654:- The helper will treat a watchdog timestamp older than 2 seconds as stale and return `HAInactive`.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2031:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6655:- That means a healthy active RG can age into `HAInactive` on the helper between watchdog refreshes.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2032:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6662:- Make the watchdog publish cadence strictly faster than the helper stale threshold, or
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2033:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6663:- stop treating the watchdog as a high-frequency liveness timer in the helper and switch to an explicit epoch/lease model with matching producer semantics.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2034:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6834:## #360 — Replace split active-plus-watchdog HA state with a single applied lease model [CLOSED] (closed 2026-04-02)
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2035:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6840:- watchdog freshness is carried separately and checked in the packet path
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2036:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6846:Failover is simpler if there is a single HA lease / generation model that the helper enforces. Separate `active` and watchdog state makes cutover semantics harder to reason about and creates extra failure modes.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2037:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6849:Replace split active-plus-watchdog HA state with one applied lease model:
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2038:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:6853:- Go refreshes / renews the same lease model instead of a second watchdog channel
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2039:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:7081:- HA state sync and watchdog updates
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2040:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:7092:3. `manager_ha.go` for HA state/watchdog/demotion/update paths
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2042:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:7706:Cached entries on the hot path can continue forwarding with a stale `ForwardCandidate`/`FabricRedirect` decision after `HAGroupRuntime::is_forwarding_active()` would already return false. That means established cached flows can keep using the local fast path after watchdog lease expiry instead of falling back to `HAInactive` and fabric redirect/slow-path re-resolution.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2043:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:8187:The `userspace_bindings` BPF map is all zeros (no registered queues), but the helper's internal status reports all queues as Registered=true, Armed=true, Ready=true. The XDP shim has nothing to redirect to, so all packets get XDP_PASS to the kernel stack, which doesn't forward transit traffic.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:2046:./docs/issues/issue-history.md:9483:  - `userspace: bindings watchdog repaired stale BPF map entries`
