     1	# xpf architecture
     2	
     3	xpf is a Junos-style stateful firewall that replicates Juniper vSRX
     4	capabilities. It has two halves:
     5	
     6	- A **Go control plane** (`xpfd`) that compiles Junos configuration,
     7	  manages sessions, drives HA, programs routing, and serves the CLI and
     8	  APIs.
     9	- A **Rust AF_XDP userspace dataplane** (`xpf-userspace-dp`) that is the
    10	  only runtime packet-forwarding path.
    11	
    12	## Dataplane: the runtime forwarding path
    13	
    14	> Dataplane notice (#1373, complete): the eBPF dataplane retirement is
    15	> done. The Rust AF_XDP userspace dataplane is the only runtime
    16	> forwarding path. Explicit `system dataplane-type ebpf` is hard-rejected
    17	> at commit (`ErrEBPFDataplaneRetired`) and at runtime
    18	> (`ErrEBPFBackendRetired`); use `set system dataplane-type userspace`, or
    19	> omit the knob for the default. The legacy BPF source (`bpf/xdp/*.c`,
    20	> `bpf/tc/*.c`) was deleted in #1476; the only retained eBPF artifacts are
    21	> the userspace XDP shim (`userspace-xdp/`) and the shared
    22	> `bpf/headers/*.h` map/struct bootstrap.
    23	
    24	A Rust forwarding engine receives packets via AF_XDP sockets and
    25	processes them in userspace. A Rust XDP shim stamps metadata, redirects
    26	transit traffic into AF_XDP, and hands proven local/control traffic back
    27	to the kernel. If helper/XSK forwarding is degraded, non-local transit
    28	fails closed in both compat and strict modes instead of bypassing
    29	policy, NAT, or conntrack.
    30	
    31	```
    32	NIC → XDP shim (redirect transit, pass local/control, drop degraded transit)
    33	    → AF_XDP socket
    34	    → Rust worker thread (session → policy → NAT → FIB → TX)
    35	    → AF_XDP TX ring → NIC
    36	```
    37	
    38	- **Per-worker architecture**: one worker per queue shard, with
    39	  session/NAT/policy/FIB handled in Rust.
    40	- **AF_XDP fast path**: supports both copy and zero-copy modes depending
    41	  on driver/path behavior.
    42	- **Kernel pass-through**: cpumap-assisted delivery keeps local/kernel-owned
    43	  traffic out of the AF_XDP fast path.
    44	- **Fail-closed admission**: unsupported userspace configs are gated or
    45	  fail closed rather than bypassing policy, NAT, or conntrack.
    46	- **Degraded mode**: when helper/XSK forwarding is unavailable, the shim
    47	  keeps non-local transit out of the kernel forwarding path, passes only
    48	  proven local/control traffic, and drops degraded transit.
    49	
    50	The parser still *accepts* the `ebpf` token so that
    51	`load merge`/`load override` of a pre-retirement config does not
    52	syntax-error during a rolling upgrade — but `commit check` then fails
    53	with the retirement error, and the remediation is
    54	`set system dataplane-type userspace`. If a persisted config still names
    55	`ebpf` on startup, the daemon runs in config-only mode until the operator
    56	updates it.
    57	
    58	To tune the userspace dataplane:
    59	
    60	```junos
    61	system {
    62	    dataplane {
    63	        binary /usr/local/sbin/xpf-userspace-dp;
    64	        workers 6;
    65	        ring-entries 8192;
    66	    }
    67	}
    68	```
    69	
    70	See [`userspace-dataplane-architecture.md`](userspace-dataplane-architecture.md)
    71	for the full architecture and [`userspace-debug-map.md`](userspace-debug-map.md)
    72	for the active debugging map. The current admission boundary is tracked
    73	in [`userspace-dataplane-gaps.md`](userspace-dataplane-gaps.md).
    74	
    75	### Historical note: the retired eBPF dataplane
    76	
    77	The original dataplane ran in-kernel using 14 BPF programs chained via
    78	tail calls (XDP ingress `main → screen → zone → conntrack → policy →
    79	nat → nat64 → forward`; TC egress `main → screen_egress → conntrack →
    80	nat → forward`) and reached 25+ Gbps on native XDP (mlx5, i40e, ice).
    81	That source (`bpf/xdp/*.c`, `bpf/tc/*.c`) was deleted in #1476; the
    82	pipeline is preserved only in git history (`git log -- bpf/xdp/ bpf/tc/`).
    83	It is no longer a selectable backend.
    84	
    85	> DPDK dataplane retired in #1525. Do not add new DPDK code. The
    86	> `dpdk_worker/` C tree and `pkg/dataplane/dpdk/` Go manager were removed
    87	> in #1527/#1528.
    88	
    89	## Key design patterns
    90	
    91	- **Go control plane** handles config compilation, session GC, management
    92	  APIs, HA cluster, and routing.
    93	- **Rust AF_XDP userspace dataplane** owns the only packet-forwarding path.
    94	- **Retained eBPF surface** is the userspace XDP shim (`userspace-xdp/`)
    95	  plus the shared `bpf/headers/*.h` map/struct bootstrap — not a
    96	  forwarding backend.
    97	- **Userspace AF_XDP shim** (`userspace-xdp/src/lib.rs`): per-CPU binding
    98	  arrays steer packets from native XDP to userspace queues.
    99	- **Dual session entries** (forward + reverse) in the shared conntrack
   100	  hash map back HA session-sync.
   101	- **Three-phase config compilation**: Junos AST → typed Go structs →
   102	  userspace-dp control messages (no eBPF map writes after #1476).
   103	- **FRR-managed routing**: all routes (static, DHCP, per-VRF) live in a
   104	  managed section in `/etc/frr/frr.conf`.
   105	- **Full interface management**: xpfd owns ALL interfaces on the firewall
   106	  — renames them via `.link` files, configures addresses/DHCP via
   107	  `.network` files, and brings down unconfigured interfaces.
   108	
   109	## Command trees (two-SSOT split, #1319)
   110	
   111	`pkg/cmdtree/tree.go` is the single source of truth for the
   112	**operational** tree (`run`/`show`/`clear`/`request`/…): tab completion
   113	and `?` help across local CLI, remote CLI, and gRPC. The **config-mode
   114	`set`/`delete`/`show`/`edit` grammar** (structural completion, flat-set
   115	token grouping, value-slot `?` completion, and commit-check typed-leaf
   116	validation) is owned by `config.setSchema` in `pkg/config/schema.go`
   117	(completion helpers in `pkg/config/schema_complete.go`) plus
   118	`config.SchemaValidate` in `pkg/config/schema_walk.go` — NOT cmdtree.
   119	Add a config-mode typed leaf by editing `setSchema` (see
   120	[`config-schema.md`](config-schema.md)); add an operational command by
   121	editing cmdtree.
   122	
   123	## APIs
   124	
   125	- **gRPC** on `127.0.0.1:50051` — 48+ RPCs (config, sessions, stats,
   126	  routes, IPsec, DHCP, cluster).
   127	- **HTTP REST** on `127.0.0.1:8080` — health, Prometheus `/metrics`,
   128	  config endpoints, full gRPC parity.
   129	- **CLI** — interactive Junos-style with tab completion, `?` help, pipe
   130	  filters (`| match`, `| count`, `| except`).
   131	- **Remote CLI** — the `cli` binary connects via gRPC with full tab/`?`
   132	  parity.
   133	
   134	## Code layout
   135	
   136	| Path | Description |
   137	|------|-------------|
   138	| `bpf/headers/*.h` | Shared C structs/constants consumed by the retained Rust AF_XDP shim build and userspace-dp parity tests. The legacy `bpf/xdp/*.c` and `bpf/tc/*.c` source were deleted in #1476 |
   139	| `pkg/config/` | Junos parser, AST, typed config, compiler |
   140	| `pkg/cmdtree/` | Single source of truth for the operational CLI command tree |
