docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16760:1. **Defect B refutation is correct.** The helper `enabled` gate is not tripped by partial bind failure. Evidence: [helpers.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/server/helpers.rs:487) says `binding.armed = armed && binding.registered`, and [helpers.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/server/helpers.rs:210) gates `enabled` on `forwarding_armed`, supported, non-empty, and `all(|b| b.registered && b.armed)`. No `bound`, `xsk_registered`, or `ready` leg is in that gate.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16762:2. **Major miss: static evidence already records post-fix 4-queue virtio success.** The plan claims the proof “does not state the channel count” ([plan.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/plan.md:115)), but [#1928 plan](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1928-virtio-copy-xsk-rx/plan.md:83) says: “Validation (venue t1921-fw, 4-queue virtio, clean production build)”, then records v4/v6 0% loss, nonzero sessions, nonzero TX completions, and 5000pps forwarding at lines 85-93. The PR ledger repeats this at [reviewer-ids.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/pr/1929-virtio-ha-gate/reviewer-ids.md:25). Phase 0 is still a sanity check, but not mandatory to decide Case 1 vs Case 2 unless later relevant code regressed.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16764:3. **The black-hole chain exists, but the plan’s READY-bit mechanism is wrong.** `queueCountFromBindings` does key on registered, not bound: [maps_sync.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/maps_sync.go:1652) skips only `!Registered || Ifindex <= 0`. But production map publishing writes `Flags: 0` unless `bindingForwardingLive` is true: [maps_sync.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/maps_sync.go:667), [maps_sync.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/maps_sync.go:691). `bindingForwardingLive` is `Registered && Armed && Ready && !deadWorkers[...]` at [maps_sync.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/maps_sync.go:97), and `Ready` requires `bound && xsk_registered && heartbeat_fresh` at [refresh_bindings.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/coordinator/refresh_bindings.rs:226). So a registered-but-unbound queue hits `binding_missing`, not `binding_not_ready`.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16766:4. **The missing-binding fallback is indeed inapplicable for the inflated same-queue case.** The fallback only runs when `flags == 0` and `selected_queue != rx_queue_index` ([lib.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-xdp/src/lib.rs:403)). With `selected_queue = rx_queue_index % queue_count` and registered queue `q < queue_count`, selected equals ingress `q`; it then drops at [lib.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-xdp/src/lib.rs:424), via `drop_degraded_transit` returning `XDP_DROP` at [lib.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-xdp/src/lib.rs:984).
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16768:5. **II-b/II-d cross-queue redirect is correctly rejected; shared UMEM does not save it.** The shim states the contract directly: “AF_XDP delivery is queue-bound” and redirecting to another userspace queue strands packets ([lib.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-xdp/src/lib.rs:1387)). Shared UMEM still creates sockets with a concrete `queue_id` ([xsk_ffi.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/xsk_ffi.rs:1178)), and virtio is explicitly excluded from shared UMEM policy ([shared_umem.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/shared_umem.rs:262)).
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16770:6. **Recommended queue-count design assumes contiguous-prefix bindability and does not prove it.** A scalar `queue_count` cannot represent “queue 1 unbound, queues 0/2/3 bound.” `rx % queue_count` at [lib.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-xdp/src/lib.rs:1395) only works if deliverable queues are `0..N-1`. The plan says “drop that queue from the plan and re-plan with the reduced queue_count” ([plan.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/plan.md:311)), but an interior failed queue either remains selected or causes cross-queue redirects. This needs a prefix proof, channel pinning, or a per-queue policy/bitmap design.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16772:7. **Do not key `queue_count` on `Ready`; `Bound` alone is also insufficient.** `Ready` includes heartbeat freshness ([refresh_bindings.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/coordinator/refresh_bindings.rs:226)), so using it makes queue topology fluctuate with liveness. `Bound` is set after socket bind ([worker/mod.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/worker/mod.rs:354)), while XSKMAP registration is separate ([worker/mod.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/worker/mod.rs:786)). If this path survives, the key should be `Bound && XSKRegistered`, plus the contiguous-prefix constraint above.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16774:8. **II-c PASS-to-kernel is a security regression against current documented behavior.** Current mode definition says `ModeUserspaceCompat` is “Userspace preferred, degraded transit fails closed” ([manager.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/manager.go:41)). Architecture docs say degraded non-local transit “fails closed in both compat and strict modes instead of bypassing policy, NAT, or conntrack” ([architecture.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/architecture.md:27)). The plan recommends PASS in non-strict ([plan.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/plan.md:262)) while leaving OQ2 open. That cannot be PLAN-READY without explicit product/security sign-off.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16776:9. **Watchdog/retry claims need tightening.** Current watchdog only detects all-queue bind wedge: `registeredArmed > 0 && bound == 0 && ready == 0` ([maps_sync.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/maps_sync.go:1285)); any partial bind makes `bound > 0`, so Phase 2 is new design, not a small extension. Retry budget is 20 attempts with 250ms sleeps ([mod.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/mod.rs:310), [bind.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/bind.rs:423)); for virtio, bind flags are just `[0]` ([bind.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/bind.rs:5)), so persistent EBUSY classification can be deterministic.
