docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16797:8. **II-c PASS-to-kernel is a security regression against current documented behavior.** Current mode definition says `ModeUserspaceCompat` is “Userspace preferred, degraded transit fails closed” ([manager.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/manager.go:41)). Architecture docs say degraded non-local transit “fails closed in both compat and strict modes instead of bypassing policy, NAT, or conntrack” ([architecture.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/architecture.md:27)). The plan recommends PASS in non-strict ([plan.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/plan.md:262)) while leaving OQ2 open. That cannot be PLAN-READY without explicit product/security sign-off.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16799:9. **Watchdog/retry claims need tightening.** Current watchdog only detects all-queue bind wedge: `registeredArmed > 0 && bound == 0 && ready == 0` ([maps_sync.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/maps_sync.go:1285)); any partial bind makes `bound > 0`, so Phase 2 is new design, not a small extension. Retry budget is 20 attempts with 250ms sleeps ([mod.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/mod.rs:310), [bind.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/bind.rs:423)); for virtio, bind flags are just `[0]` ([bind.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/afxdp/bind.rs:5)), so persistent EBUSY classification can be deterministic.
docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/codex-plan-r1.log:16801:I did not modify files. The worktree already has an untracked `docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/claude-smr-plan-r1.md`.

codex
