   138	stop fixes the EBUSY loop AND these two latent rebind bugs. Safe for the
   139	RETH-MAC link-cycle path: Go already sends `stop_workers` (→
   140	`stop_workers::handle` → `afxdp.stop()`) before the link cycle
   141	(`process.go:959`), waits 1s, and sends `rebind` after link-up
   142	(`process.go:1018`); the hardware-teardown cleanup remains covered.
