   348	  `queue_planner_uses_smallest_queue_count`, `main_tests.rs:609-631`). So the
   349	  reconciliation MUST produce one uniform target that every dataplane NIC
   350	  actually RSS-honors; a per-interface "bind all of NIC B's queues" is
   351	  unimplementable without reworking the planner. Definition:
   352	  - `target = min(workers, min hw-max-combined across reconcilable dataplane
   353	    NICs)` — uniform.
   354	  - For each dataplane NIC (fabric/generic parents excluded — hazard 5), make it
   355	    deliver only to `0..target-1`: prefer `ethtool -L combined target`; if the
   356	    driver lacks `-L` (many VFs), fall back to constraining the **RSS
   357	    indirection table** via `ethtool -X` to `0..target-1` (the codebase already
   358	    drives `-X`, `rss_indirection.go`). Either achieves "NIC delivers only to
   359	    the bound queues."
   360	  - If a NIC supports NEITHER `-L` nor `-X` and natively delivers on more than
   361	    `target`, uniformity is impossible without dropping its high-queue traffic.
   362	    Out of scope: **require homogeneous, constrainable dataplane NICs** (true for
   363	    both venues — all-virtio appliance, all-mlx5 loss). Document this limit; do
   364	    not silently clamp (the wrong-ring drop).
   365	  - The reconciliation is **transactional**: compute `target`, apply to all
   366	    dataplane NICs, verify each honors it, THEN build the snapshot stamping
   367	    `rx_queues = target` uniformly. Rust binds `0..target-1` (global-min planner
   368	    unchanged). Since Rust trusts `snapshot.rx_queues` (`helpers.rs:698`), the
   369	    pin/RSS-constrain must complete in Go before snapshot construction
   370	    (Codex #2/#3); a helper-side recompute is too late.
   371	- `replan_queues` signature unchanged; its queue-count source becomes the
   372	  snapshot's uniform reconciled `target`, not raw sysfs.
   373	- Operator-facing `workers` semantics unchanged; document the new
   374	  channel-reconciliation behavior.
   375	
   376	## 7. Hidden invariants the change must preserve
   377	
   378	- **Ordering:** channel-set MUST precede any XSK bind and MUST follow
   379	  `stop_workers` on reconcile, or it hits the "channels too low for existing ZC
   380	  sockets" EINVAL (the live symptom). 
   381	- **mlx5/i40e no-op:** `combined=workers` must be a no-op when already equal;
   382	  never reduce a NIC that legitimately wants more queues than `workers` if the
   383	  config intends full fan-out (decide: does Path A clamp mlx5 to workers? On
   384	  loss workers=6=queues so equal — but assert no reduction below the configured
   385	  fan-out).
   386	- **HA / fabric:** fabric parent (ge-0-0-0, xdpgeneric) needs ≥1 TX queue; the
   387	  channel-pin must not zero it. RETH MAC link-cycle path already does
   388	  stop_workers — the pin must integrate with that sequence, not race it.
   389	- **Heartbeat/ready gating** unchanged; the shim's per-queue READY + heartbeat
   390	  path stays.
