commit 76e78848ae2b71c27235c24708daa30175049216
Author: Paul Saab <ps@mu.org>
Date:   Mon Jun 15 16:45:00 2026 -0700

    #1921: rebind must not double-stop workers (fixes virtio-MQ EBUSY loop)
    
    rebind::handle called guard.afxdp.stop() before reconcile_status_bindings.
    afxdp.stop() runs stop_inner(true), which clears coord.workers.handles. The
    reconcile pipeline's tear_down then samples
    `had_live_workers = !coord.workers.handles.is_empty()` and, finding it false,
    SKIPS the 500ms zero-copy teardown quiesce (coordinator/reconcile/teardown.rs).
    The freshly recreated AF_XDP sockets then race the kernel's still-pending
    xsk_pool teardown and fail with EBUSY ("Device or resource busy"). On a
    virtio_net multi-queue NIC the busy-binding watchdog re-issues rebind, which
    double-stops and bypasses the quiesce again — an infinite EBUSY/rebind loop
    that leaves every queue un-READY, so the shim drops all transit
    (binding_not_ready) and the appliance forwards nothing.
    
    Remove the explicit stop from rebind::handle and let reconcile (-> tear_down ->
    stop_inner(false)) own the worker stop, so had_live_workers is captured
    truthfully and the quiesce applies. This also drops stop_inner(true)'s two
    side effects that are wrong for a rebind: wiping the in-memory synced-session
    map (which should be replayed into BPF maps on bringup) and defaulting
    coord.forwarding/coord.validation before tear_down captures
    tunnel_owners/snapshot_was_installed (which blinded the tunnel-owner remap
    purge in apply_snapshot across all rebinds).
    
    The RETH-MAC link-cycle path is unaffected: Go sends a separate stop_workers
    request before the link cycle (process.go) and only issues rebind after
    link-up.
    
    Adds a server-level regression (rebind_preserves_synced_sessions) that pins the
    observable consequence: a synced session installed before a rebind survives it.
    Verified the test fails if the explicit stop is re-added. Diagnosis converged
    through a 6-round 3-way hostile plan review (Codex + AGY + Claude SMR); the
    channel/RSS reconciliation half is deferred to a contingent Phase 2 (#1921
    plan §5/§6) pending a live virtio repro showing it is needed.
