**Verdict: PLAN-READY.** Accept the PLAN-KILL for the original #1921 forwarding outage.

The decisive validation is real: [plan.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1928-virtio-copy-xsk-rx/plan.md:83) says `t1921-fw` was a “4-queue virtio” venue; lines 85-93 show v4/v6 0% loss, nonzero sessions/BPF entries, `tx_completions_total` nonzero across LAN+WAN bindings, SNAT proof, and sustained `rx≈tx≈fwd=5000` with `ha_inact=0`, `tx_err=0`. That kills the reported “4-channel virtio forwards nothing” bug.

Could RSS have masked a stranded queue? In isolation, yes: #1928 does not dump per-queue counters for every binding. But I do not see a blocking current-master counterexample. The current live-cause fixes remove the known ways to create the stranded queue: #1927’s dedup fix is captured in the commit/test context and the current planner dedups by Linux netdev, while [helpers.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/server/helpers.rs:759) still plans the contiguous `0..queue_count` queue set. The remaining “registered-but-unbound queue receives RSS traffic” path is real, but r2 correctly treats it as latent durability hardening, not the still-reproducing #1921 outage.

All r1 findings are folded:

- `queue_count` follow-up is now `max(QueueID where Bound && XSKRegistered)+1`, not count and not `Ready`: [plan.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/plan.md:109).
- PASS-to-kernel is rejected; fail-closed DROP + observability matches [docs/architecture.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/architecture.md:27) and [manager.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/manager.go:41).
- Interior holes are explicitly documented as not representable by scalar `queue_count`: [plan.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/plan.md:122).
- Global-rebind watchdog extension is rejected; current watchdog only fires when `bound == 0`: [maps_sync.go](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/pkg/dataplane/userspace/maps_sync.go:1285), and r2 rejects the design at [plan.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/plan.md:147).

Closing #1921 is the right call. Defect A is refuted as the live cause at [plan.md](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/docs/research/1921-queue-arm-gate/plan.md:50); Defect B-as-written is refuted by the arm gate semantics at [helpers.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/server/helpers.rs:485) and the enabled gate at [helpers.rs](/home/ps/git/bpfrx/.claude/worktrees/1921-research-queue-arm-gate/userspace-dp/src/server/helpers.rs:210). The durability follow-up should be separate, low-priority hardening. No files modified.
